// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6542 Add Linux rule: Potential Shell Or Command Execution Via Tar
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6542
// Pull request author: rafaelsoje
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Shell Or Command Execution Via Tar
// Sigma ID: 5fbd1c84-c13d-414a-9ab5-c20e40a122f5
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Rafael Soje (@rafaelsoje)
// Date: 2026-10-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, T1059.004, T1548.003
// Description: Detects the execution of commands or interactive shells using the "tar" utility via flags such
//   as "--checkpoint-action=exec" or "--to-command". This is a GTFOBins technique commonly abused in
//   wildcard injection attacks, sudoers misconfigurations, or restricted shell escapes to execute
//   arbitrary code with elevated privileges.
// False positives:
//   - Highly unlikely in production environments. Reading from archives with "--to-command" or invoking shell execution on checkpoints via "--checkpoint-action=exec" is rarely used in legitimate automation.
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/tar/
//   - https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2014/06/27/exploiting-wildcards-on-linux/
//   - https://book.hacktricks.wiki/en/linux-hardening/privilege-escalation/wildcards-spare-tricks.html#tar
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9807b4958abd821826a2727328309e61d0ef5c1b/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_tar_shell_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/tar" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-action=exec" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-action exec" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-action=\"exec" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-action='exec" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command=" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command " or ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command=\"" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command='")
